# The rename pass against the stress corpus: 558 targets of macro-heavy,
# template-heavy C++. googletest is the corpus the rename work was developed
# against; abseil is the independent one, and it still finds things.
#
# 2982 edits apply and 546 of the 558 targets rebuild, but 753 errors remain in
# 12 files. Every one is the same shape -- a member renamed at its declaration
# whose use was not rewritten -- from at least two distinct causes.
#
#   Textual headers (24 errors). absl/log/log_basic_test_impl.inc is listed in
#   textual_hdrs, not in srcs or hdrs, so the aspect never passes it and its
#   reference to LogEntry::kNoVerbosityLevel is invisible. A limitation of the
#   Bazel integration rather than of the rename.
#
#   A dependent-token veto that does not reach its declaration (StatusOr, and
#   part of raw_hash_set). Reduced to:
#
#     template <class T> struct Data { union { Status status_; }; };
#     template <class T> struct StatusOr : Data<T> {
#       bool ok() const { return this->status_.ok(); }
#     };
#
#   status_ renames, this->status_ does not. The member is declared in an
#   ANONYMOUS UNION, so in the instantiation the resolved field cannot be
#   mapped back to the pattern; the recorder concludes the token binds to a
#   member this rule is not renaming and vetoes the token. That veto is keyed
#   on the TOKEN, not on the declaration -- vetoResolution() records no owner --
#   so aggregation drops only the token's edit and the declaration's rename
#   survives. Neither half alone reproduces: a plain member of a dependent base
#   rewrites correctly across TUs, and an anonymous union member used inside its
#   own class rewrites correctly too.
#
#   str_format extension.h (147) and any_span.h (24) are not yet diagnosed and
#   have no anonymous union, so expect a third cause.
#
# Kept as a known_fail rather than narrowed until it passes: these are the
# cases the googletest corpus does not contain.
#
# NB: this file is sourced by bash, so values must not contain backticks or the
# dollar sign.
REPO=abseil-cpp
RULESET=member_snake_case
EXPECT=known_fail
EXPECT_FAIL_PHASE=rebuild
EXPECT_FAIL_REASON='753 errors in 12 files, all of them a member renamed at its declaration whose use was missed. 24 come from a textual_hdrs .inc the aspect never passes. The rest are dependent tokens that were vetoed without the veto reaching the declaration: a member declared in an anonymous union cannot be mapped back to its pattern from an instantiation, so the token is vetoed while the declaration still renames. vetoResolution() records no owner, so aggregation cannot drop the declaration too.'
